-- title:
--   The quotient j-invariant is a class function on Y₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $N$ a nonzero natural number with $(N : L) \neq 0$, and let $P$ and $Q$ be two $\Gamma_0(N)$-pairs over $L$, i.e. data consisting of a Weierstrass curve `toCurve` over $L$ together with a proof that it is elliptic and a point `gen` of its affine point group whose additive order is exactly $N$. Assume that $P$ and $Q$ have the same image in [`ModularCurve.ModuliPoint N L`](def/ModularCurve_ModuliPoint.html#L35), the quotient of the type of $\Gamma_0(N)$-pairs by the relation `Gamma0Pair.Step`, which holds for a pair $(P,Q)$ when there are a Weierstrass variable change $\gamma$ over $L$ with $\gamma \cdot P.\mathrm{toCurve} = Q.\mathrm{toCurve}$ and a natural number $k$ coprime to $N$ such that $Q.\mathrm{gen}$ agrees (as a heterogeneous equality, the curves being identified by the first condition) with $k \cdot \mathrm{vcInvFun}\,\gamma\,(P.\mathrm{gen})$, the image of $P.\mathrm{gen}$ under the coordinate substitution. Let $d$ be a natural number dividing $N$. Then the two quantities $\mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}$, namely $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the curve obtained from $P.\mathrm{toCurve}$ by the iterated cyclic quotient construction of parameter $d$ at the subgroup generated by $(N/d) \cdot P.\mathrm{gen}$, and the corresponding quantity for $Q$, are equal.
--
--   This is the well-definedness, on the moduli set underlying $Y_0(N)$, of the $j$-invariant of the quotient of an elliptic curve by the order-$d$ subgroup of the cyclic group generated by the marked point of order $N$: it says that $[(E,g)] \mapsto j\bigl(E/\langle (N/d)g\rangle\bigr)$ depends only on the class and not on the chosen Weierstrass model or on the choice of generator. It is used where points of the moduli set are evaluated against the quotient invariant, in particular in the identification of such values with $j(q^d)$ for Tate curves at full level.
-- source:
